<title>JAPAN: Nisseki House shares slip on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Nisseki House shares slip on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nisseki House Industry Co Ltd slipped on profit-taking in Tuesday morning trade.</p>
<p>The shares ended the morning session at 310 yen, down 30 yen from the Monday close, in turnover of 3.05 million. Nisseki House was the biggest percentage loser on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The company's share had recently rebounded on buying by speculators. The share had been losing ground on news that it had not been able to contact its president since early December.</p>
</text>
